WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:16.916
The term at Redmond sped by as quickly as the first, and Anne enjoyed it thoroughly.

2
00:00:18.477 --> 00:00:21.918
She studied hard, for she wanted to win a scholarship in English.

3
00:00:22.878 --> 00:00:27.959
If she won it, the scholarship would pay for her tuition fees at Redmond College next year, and

4
00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:29.920
she would not have to use Marilla's savings.

5
00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:36.377
Gilbert, too, was hoping to get a scholarship, but he still found plenty of time to drop in

6
00:00:36.437 --> 00:00:38.038
and visit Anne at her boardinghouse.

7
00:00:39.158 --> 00:00:44.640
He was Anne's escort to most college events, and Anne knew students gossiped about them being a "couple."

8
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.621
The gossip made Anne furious, but she could not refuse Gilbert's company.

9
00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:55.803
He was her old friend, and she would feel bad declining his kind offers to accompany her to

10
00:00:55.843 --> 00:00:56.543
college events.

11
00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:00.584
Besides, he had stopped acting like a suitor toward her.

12
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:05.623
Anne was very glad of that, though she did secretly wonder why he'd changed.

13
00:01:06.764 --> 00:01:09.386
Only one disagreeable incident spoiled that winter.

14
00:01:11.007 --> 00:01:14.770
One night Charlie Sloane asked Anne if she would promise "to become Mrs.

15
00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.271
Charlie Sloane some day."

16
00:01:17.372 --> 00:01:20.214
Of course, Anne knew that she could never marry Charlie.

17
00:01:21.274 --> 00:01:24.157
After all, he was not her romantic hero either!

18
00:01:24.177 --> 00:01:27.679
"Another unromantic proposal!"

19
00:01:28.099 --> 00:01:28.680
Anne sighed.

20
00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:31.690
"Where is my Prince Charming?"

21
00:01:33.891 --> 00:01:36.473
The next day Anne scurried into Priscilla's room.

22
00:01:36.493 --> 00:01:44.278
"Read that," she cried, tossing Priscilla a letter from Stella Maynard, who had been one of their friends

23
00:01:44.338 --> 00:01:45.219
at Queen's College.

24
00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.741
"Stella is coming to Redmond to study next year.

25
00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.363
Tell me what you think of her idea.

26
00:01:52.403 --> 00:01:54.945
I think it's wonderful, if it's possible."

27
00:01:54.965 --> 00:01:59.008
"Anne, I have a little plan," Stella had written.

28
00:01:59.904 --> 00:02:01.385
"You know how I hate boarding.

29
00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:04.868
I've boarded for four years and I'm so sick of it.

30
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.352
I can imagine you are not a huge fan of boardinghouses either.

31
00:02:10.313 --> 00:02:15.177
Why don't you and Priscilla and I rent a little house somewhere in Halifax?"

32
00:02:15.197 --> 00:02:19.521
"I think it's a good idea," said Priscilla after she read the letter.

33
00:02:19.541 --> 00:02:23.164
"So do I," agreed Anne delightedly.

34
00:02:23.184 --> 00:02:27.428
"Let's go house-hunting at once, before exams start."

35
00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.862
"I'm afraid it will be hard to get a house that fits our budget," warned Priscilla.

36
00:02:32.882 --> 00:02:36.303
"We'll have to be happy with a shabby little place."

37
00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:43.046
Over the next few days, they saw many houses, but they were either too big, too small, too

38
00:02:43.106 --> 00:02:45.407
expensive, or too far from Redmond.

39
00:02:46.227 --> 00:02:48.088
The house-hunting was not going well.

40
00:02:50.589 --> 00:02:56.371
A few weeks later, Anne and Priscilla were walking home the usual way, down Spofford Avenue, so that

41
00:02:56.411 --> 00:02:57.812
they could look at Patty's Place.

42
00:02:59.484 --> 00:03:04.348
As they stopped to admire the garden, Anne suddenly shouted, "Look, look!

43
00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:06.630
Am I seeing things, Priscilla?

44
00:03:07.431 --> 00:03:09.793
Look over there and tell me if it's true!"

45
00:03:10.594 --> 00:03:12.396
Priscilla looked where Anne was pointing.

46
00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:17.840
Over the arched gateway of Patty's Place dangled a little sign.

47
00:03:18.621 --> 00:03:20.262
It said "For Rent.

48
00:03:20.683 --> 00:03:22.905
Furnished. Inquire Within."

49
00:03:22.925 --> 00:03:29.494
"Priscilla," said Anne in a whisper, "is it possible we could rent Patty's Place?"

50
00:03:29.514 --> 00:03:32.256
"It's too good to be true, Anne.

51
00:03:33.237 --> 00:03:39.241
Fairy tales don't happen nowadays But then again maybe they do," Priscilla replied excitedly.

52
00:03:39.261 --> 00:03:43.324
"Anyway, it's too late to knock on their door this evening.

53
00:03:44.204 --> 00:03:45.405
Let's come back tomorrow."

54
00:03:46.566 --> 00:03:49.688
Early the next evening, the girls went back to Patty's Place.

55
00:03:50.509 --> 00:03:54.632
They knocked on the door rather timidly, and then stepped into a large living room.

56
00:03:55.536 --> 00:03:57.317
Two old ladies sat by the fire.

57
00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:03.779
They were very similar, except that one looked about seventy years old and the other fifty.

58
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:09.302
They were both knitting, and the older one invited Anne and Priscilla to take a seat.

59
00:04:10.242 --> 00:04:16.064
Behind each lady sat a large white china dog, with a green nose and ears and green spots

60
00:04:16.164 --> 00:04:16.625
all over.

61
00:04:17.585 --> 00:04:22.067
Anne liked the dogs straight away; they seemed to her like the guardians of Patty's Place.

62
00:04:23.187 --> 00:04:24.808
For a few minutes nobody spoke.

63
00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:31.244
The girls were too nervous, and the ladies were content to knit and wait for their guests to

64
00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.005
speak first.

65
00:04:33.226 --> 00:04:34.547
Anne glanced about the room.

66
00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.789
What a nice place it was!

67
00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:38.911
Finally she spoke.

68
00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:46.197
"We we saw your sign that this house is for rent," said Anne to the older lady.

69
00:04:46.217 --> 00:04:49.459
"Oh, yes," said Miss Patty.

70
00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:52.982
"I meant to take that sign down today."

71
00:04:54.984 --> 00:04:55.924
"Oh, are we too late?"

72
00:04:56.364 --> 00:04:58.865
asked Anne, barely hiding her disappointment.

73
00:04:58.885 --> 00:05:01.786
"No," Miss Patty said.

74
00:05:01.806 --> 00:05:05.507
"We have decided not to rent it after all."

75
00:05:05.527 --> 00:05:07.888
"What a shame!"

76
00:05:08.348 --> 00:05:09.248
exclaimed Anne.

77
00:05:09.268 --> 00:05:11.789
"I love this place so much.

78
00:05:12.569 --> 00:05:14.510
I really hoped we could have lived here."

79
00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.311
"You love it?"

80
00:05:16.791 --> 00:05:17.611
said Miss Patty.

81
00:05:17.631 --> 00:05:20.852
"I really do love it," Anne said.

82
00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.101
"I've loved it ever since I first saw it last fall."

83
00:05:25.121 --> 00:05:29.543
"You're not just saying that you 'love it'?

84
00:05:30.403 --> 00:05:34.464
Young people 'love' everything these days," said Miss Patty.

85
00:05:34.484 --> 00:05:37.925
"No, I really adore this house.

86
00:05:38.845 --> 00:05:41.726
Priscilla and I walk by it often," Anne said.

87
00:05:41.746 --> 00:05:46.368
"If you love it, you can have it," said Miss Patty.

88
00:05:47.332 --> 00:05:53.237
"I decided today that I wouldn't rent it because we didn't like any of the people who asked

89
00:05:53.277 --> 00:05:53.898
to rent it.

90
00:05:54.799 --> 00:05:55.679
You are different.

91
00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:59.543
I believe you do love it and will take care of it."

92
00:05:59.563 --> 00:06:03.626
"If if we can afford the rent.

93
00:06:04.547 --> 00:06:07.430
We have a limited budget," said Anne meekly.

94
00:06:08.531 --> 00:06:10.032
Miss Patty named the amount.

95
00:06:11.093 --> 00:06:14.356
Anne and Priscilla looked at each other, and Priscilla shook her head.

96
00:06:15.592 --> 00:06:20.035
"I'm afraid we can't afford it," said Anne, choking back her disappointment.

97
00:06:20.055 --> 00:06:23.178
"We're only students and we're poor."

98
00:06:23.198 --> 00:06:25.980
"What can you afford?"

99
00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.220
asked Miss Patty.

100
00:06:28.341 --> 00:06:30.923
Anne named her amount and Miss Patty nodded.

101
00:06:30.943 --> 00:06:32.504
"That will do.

102
00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:34.085
You can move in.

103
00:06:34.926 --> 00:06:38.108
We leave in two months, at the start of next term.

104
00:06:39.049 --> 00:06:43.232
You don't object, I hope, to this house being called Patty's Place?"

105
00:06:44.257 --> 00:06:48.284
"No, that's one of the nicest things about it," Anne said, smiling.

106
00:06:49.205 --> 00:06:50.728
Patty's Place was theirs.

107
00:06:51.709 --> 00:06:54.174
At least one small dream had come true!
